The '''2000 FIFA Club World Championship final''' was an [[association football]] match that took place at [[Maracanã Stadium|Estádio do Maracanã]], [[Rio de Janeiro]] on 14 January 2000. It was an all-Brazilian final between [[Sport Club Corinthians Paulista|Corinthians]] and [[CR Vasco da Gama|Vasco da Gama]] to determine the winner of the [[2000 FIFA Club World Championship]]. After a goalless 120 minutes, Corinthians won the penalty shoot-out 4–3, becoming the first club to lift the FIFA Club World Cup.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/special_report/1999/12/99/world_club_championship/604434.stm|title=Corinthians crowned world champions|date=15 January 2000|publisher=BBC Sport|accessdate= 6 May 2021}}</ref>

